@!internal

--- The native core's scheduler primitives, under the scheduler written in
--- Nupp (`nupp.runtime.scheduler`). A call of one is the core's own library
--- call (TASKS, its operation first, numbered once in
--- `nupp.compiler.vm.corelibrary`), and requiring this module loads nothing:
--- it exists only on the core.
local record taskcalls
    --- A task calling `body` with the arguments of the pack `arguments`, not
    --- yet run.
    new: function(body: any, arguments: any): any

    --- Runs `task` until it returns, fails, parks or gives up its turn: a pack
    --- whose first value says which (1 to 4) and the rest what came with it,
    --- its park answering `value`.
    run: function(task: any, value: any): any

    --- Parks the running task, answering what its driver runs it again with,
    --- or false at once where no task runs.
    park: function(): any

    --- The running task, or nil.
    current: function(): any

    --- A task's record, and setting it to `record`.
    data: function(task: any): any

    setdata: function(task: any, record: any): any

    --- The monotonic clock in milliseconds.
    now: function(): any

    --- Waits `milliseconds` milliseconds.
    sleep: function(milliseconds: any): any

    --- Installs `metatable` as every thread's metatable and `close` as the
    --- function closing a task.
    install: function(metatable: any, close: any): any
end

local calls: taskcalls
return calls
